# Cuboidy files have a canonical byte form: the serializers emit `\n`, and the
# test suite asserts a byte-level fixed point on every shipped model (parse →
# serialize must reproduce the file exactly). A platform-rewritten working tree
# breaks that — with `core.autocrlf=true`, a Windows checkout hands the reader
# CRLF files that every tool then rewrites to LF, so `cuboidy-part` or a save
# from the editor shows the whole file as changed.
#
# So the working tree is LF everywhere, on every platform. Nothing in this repo
# is Windows-specific (no .bat/.cmd/.ps1), so there is nothing to exempt.
* text=auto eol=lf
